  "description": "Stage W2b: a service's dwell at each call, second by second (x10, one second a tick). Track a(0,1)-b(1,1)-c(2,1)-d(3,1)-e(4,1)-f(5,1)-g(6,1); Alpha(1,0) has platform b, Beta(3,0) d, Gamma(5,0) f. Local (rate 1024, one link a minute, so two links take 120 s) runs Alpha 0/2, Beta 3/3, Gamma 6/7 (minutes), with no passengers. Starting at 0 counts as arriving at Alpha at 0. The doors take 8 s to open: the step at 8 lets passengers off and on (none, so the exchange ends at 8). Alpha is a terminal (the first stop), least dwell 42 s, but the train is early: its doors start closing 9 s before its departure, at 111, and it leaves at 120, on time. It reaches Beta at 240 (scheduled 180): 60 s late while it waits. Beta is between the ends, least dwell 36 s: no hold for the timetable, the doors close at 240 + 36 - 9 = 267 and it leaves at 276, 96 s late, which it stays while travelling. It reaches Gamma at 396, 36 s after its scheduled arrival; there it waits for its scheduled departure at 420 (lateness 0 until then), but Gamma is the last stop (least dwell 42 s), so its doors close at 396 + 42 - 9 = 429 and the service ends at 438, 18 s late. Each event happens in the step at its second, so a batch that ends at that second has not seen it yet.",
